WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.600
Window functions are different from GROUP BY because
they can add analytical

00:00:03.625 --> 00:00:08.900
information while keeping the detail rows GROUP BY
usually collapses many input

00:00:08.925 --> 00:00:13.162
rows into one row per group If we group employees by
department

00:00:13.362 --> 00:00:17.838
we lose the individual employee rows unless we do
additional work A

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:21.775
window function can calculate something such as
department average salary and place

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:27.362
that value beside every employee row The detail
remains visible The

00:00:27.388 --> 00:00:32.513
OVER clause defines the window PARTITION BY creates
groups for the calculation

00:00:32.538 --> 00:00:37.362
without collapsing the rows ORDER BY inside OVER can
define the sequence

00:00:37.375 --> 00:00:41.925
for ranking or running totals This makes window
functions useful for rank

00:00:42.138 --> 00:00:47.000
running totals moving averages comparisons with
group averages and many other analytical

00:00:47.025 --> 00:00:51.325
tasks A simple question can help you choose between
GROUP BY and

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:55.425
a window function If you want one row per group
GROUP BY

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:59.275
is often appropriate If you want to keep each
original row and

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:03.925
add group-level context a window function is often
the better tool The

00:01:03.938 --> 00:01:06.388
next examples will make that difference visible
